**Finding: compliant** (no redline proposed).

The agreement contains no non-solicitation, no-hire, or anti-poaching covenant. Full-text searches for "solicit", "hire", "induce", "recruit", "personnel", "engage" and "compete" surfaced only:

- **p0051** — indemnity reference to "HDI, its employees, or agents" (no hiring restriction);
- **p0061** — Section 10.2 No Joint Venture (independent-contractor status only);
- **p0045** — Section 7.2 Mutual Covenants as to Advertisements (advertising compliance, unrelated).

Since nothing restricts the Company from soliciting or hiring HDI personnel, the document sits at our **preferred** position ("No non-solicit on Customer"), so this is compliant rather than missing — the rule's ideal outcome is the absence of such a clause. No action needed unless HDI later proposes one, in which case the fallback (mutual, service-involved personnel only, 12 months, general-advertising and unsolicited-approach carve-outs, no no-hire) would be our target.
